{"id":"G5610","lemma":"ὥρα","transliteration":"hōra","sayIt":"hōra","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"noun, feminine","gloss":"hour","meaning":"ὥρα, -ας, ἡ,\n[in LXX chiefly for עֵת and in Da for שָׁעָה ;]\n1. any time or period fixed by nature, esp. a season (Hom., Hdt., Plat., al.).\n2. A part of the day, and esp. a twelfth part of day or night, an hour: Mat.24:36, Mrk.13:32, Act.10:3, al.; accus. in ans. to \"when\"? (M, Pr., 63, 215; Bl., §34, 8), Jhn.4:52, Act.10:3, 30 1Co.15:30, Rev.3:3; accusative of duration, Mat.20:12 26, Mrk.14:37; inexactly, πρὸς ὥραν, for a season, for a time, Jhn.5:35, 2Co.7:8, Gal.2:5; πρὸς καιρὸν ὥρας, for a short season (ICC, in l.), 1Th.2:17.\n3. A definite point of time, time, hour: Mat.26:45; with genitive of thing(s), Luk.1:10 14:17, Rev.3:10, al.; with genitive of person(s), Luk.22:53, Jhn.2:4 7:30, al.; ἡ ἄρτι ὥρα, 1Co.4:11; ἐσχάτη ὥ., 1Jn.2:18; before ὅτε, Jhn.4:21, 23 5:25 16:25; ἵνα, Jhn.12:23, al.; with accusative and inf., Rom.13:11 (cf. DB, ext., 475b 476b).\n(AS)","glosses":["hour","time","moment","hours","short time","it"],"count":99,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"mat-8","v":13,"renderings":{"bsb":"hour"}},{"chapterId":"mat-9","v":22,"renderings":{"bsb":"hour"}},{"chapterId":"mat-10","v":19,"renderings":{"bsb":"hour","kjv":"hour"}},{"chapterId":"mat-14","v":15,"renderings":{"bsb":"hour","kjv":"the time"}},{"chapterId":"mat-15","v":28,"renderings":{"bsb":"hour"}},{"chapterId":"mat-17","v":18,"renderings":{"bsb":"moment"}},{"chapterId":"mat-18","v":1,"renderings":{"bsb":"time","kjv":"time"}},{"chapterId":"mat-20","v":3,"renderings":{"bsb":"hour","kjv":"hour"}},{"chapterId":"mat-20","v":5,"renderings":{"bsb":"hour","kjv":"hour"}},{"chapterId":"mat-20","v":9,"renderings":{"bsb":"hour","kjv":"hour"}},{"chapterId":"mat-20","v":12,"renderings":{"bsb":"hour","kjv":"our"}},{"chapterId":"mat-24","v":36,"renderings":{"bsb":"hour","kjv":"hour"}},{"chapterId":"mat-24","v":44,"renderings":{"bsb":"hour","kjv":"an hour"}},{"chapterId":"